WEBVTT

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:14.610
Seriously?

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.490
Youichi?

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:31.020
Youichi!

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:07.640
He's got a bad fever.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:13.400
We never should've gone to Kobe if
something like this was gonna happen.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:18.910
I shouldn't've said I wanted that meat bun...

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:21.410
I should've stopped him too.

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:23.530
Last night, Youichi was prac—

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:24.410
Stop.

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:27.160
Maruyama, what did you just say?

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:29.170
Well, that was...

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:31.090
What did you do?

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:33.410
I practiced in the hotel's pool.

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:36.990
And I lost track of the time, that's all.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:40.090
Why would you do something so stupid at an important time like this?

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:43.130
Being stupid at the worst moment is a hobby of mine.

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:44.160
Quit screwing around!

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:49.600
You were on the verge of hitting your limit with your SS Special training.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:53.480
Practicing the night before competition? How suicidal could you be?!

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:55.680
You should've known better!

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:57.610
Then what about you?!

00:02:58.390 --> 00:02:59.360
Me?

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:04.560
For you, all that matters is getting one of us to the Olympics, right?

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:07.920
And if you do, you could rest easy and go home to America.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:13.000
But only one person gets to advance from today's meet to the Tokyo Olympics.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:15.960
There's gonna be more losers than winners.

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:23.510
I thought that you would stick around whether you accomplished your goal or not, for the sake of the losers.

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:25.760
I mean, you said it yourself!

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:27.770
There's another Olympics in five years!

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:30.770
Hold on a second, what are you talking—

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:32.270
I haven't seen it yet!

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:33.270
What?

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:38.320
Coach, didn't you say that there was a view only I could see?

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:41.030
I haven't seen it yet.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:43.930
That's right!

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:46.410
Stay here to show Tomo that!

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:52.540
You're fully aware of your talent as a coach, and how much we all need you, right?!

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:55.750
You're a pain as always, Fujitani.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:00.050
In other words, he's saying, "Asaki Kayoko is essential to MDC.

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:03.040
Don't leave for America."

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:04.050
And I feel the same.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:07.560
Don't just run away after making a
man care about something so much!

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:08.810
Huh?

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:11.560
There are so many more things I want you to teach me.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:15.060
The independent training regimen you
gave us almost made me throw up at first,

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:17.570
but now it's not enough!

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:18.630
You too!

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:20.680
Come on.

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:21.820
Say something.

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:28.830
I'd like to keep learning from you too, Coach Asaki.

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:30.180
Thanks.

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:33.080
I'm happy to know how you all feel, but—

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:34.580
No buts!

00:04:34.930 --> 00:04:36.950
Wait. Hear me out.

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:40.370
I never said I was going to America.

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:41.030
What?

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:44.590
I overheard you talking about going to America, though.

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:46.680
Oh, I see.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:49.600
I wasn't talking about myself.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:52.350
Then... who?

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:56.850
That was about you, Okitsu.

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:58.860
Me?

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:03.870
In Florida, there's a doctor named Ben Bradley who's said to be the authority on sports medical science.

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:10.060
An expert who's brought countless athletes,
who other doctors had given up on, back to the top.

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:12.770
I was thinking of having you go see him.

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:19.130
When I told Ben about you,
he said you should come to Florida right away.

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:20.580
That's great!

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:27.130
If I heal my back in Florida,
will I be able to compete on the huge worldwide stage?

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:28.160
Yes.

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:31.140
Will I be able to keep diving with them for years to come?

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:32.520
Of course.

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:35.140
You're only seventeen, after all.

00:05:35.450 --> 00:05:38.180
However, just doing so comes with its own costs.

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:42.400
So I had a discussion with Chairman Maebara from the JSF.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:43.900
With Chairman Maebara?

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:48.500
Yep, about making an investment in the upbringing of future medalists.

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:54.360
Depending on certain factors, he said he could let
you do Japan's first study abroad training program.

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:55.910
He promised that.

00:05:55.910 --> 00:05:57.960
What are those certain factors?

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:59.670
Let me finish.

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:06.170
Chairman Maebara will decide whether
he'll invest in you or not in today's meet.

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:10.180
Got it.

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:12.710
Yes.

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:15.480
Understood. I'll be right there.

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:19.910
Now, it's time to prepare for the finals.

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:23.190
Can you do it, Fujitani?

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:24.710
Of course.

00:06:24.710 --> 00:06:27.200
I've just engaged my battle mode.

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:28.950
I'm suddenly ready to do this.

00:06:29.230 --> 00:06:30.760
Let's go, then!

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:31.950
Yes, ma'am!

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:34.450
Hey.

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:40.960
I'll now introduce the participating divers.

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:43.960
Moriya Kazuki, Ishikawa Diving Club.

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:46.960
Maruyama Reiji, Mizuki Diving Club.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:49.970
Kaburagi Shinji, Chubu Sports University.

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:52.470
Hirayama Jirou, Splash Osaka.

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:55.700
Asama Takashi, Mishio University.

00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:56.470
Nakayama Masahiko...

00:06:56.470 --> 00:07:00.870
Isn't Tomo amazing? If he wins today, he might go on to the Olympics.

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:02.730
This was all he gave any effort to.

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:04.980
I can't help but root for him.

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:06.980
What a relief!

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:09.480
Looks like Youichi's all right.

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:12.100
I'm sure he'd dive whether or not he was all right.

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:13.990
That's the kind of guy he is.

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:16.490
Yeah, you're right.

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:36.540
Doesn't it seem like the Tomo over there is
completely different from the one we know?

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:38.660
It really does.

00:07:38.660 --> 00:07:39.770
I hope he wins.

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:45.980
<i>Your diving is stiff, Reiji.</i>

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:49.530
<i>It's okay to be careful, but add some flavor to it.</i>

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:54.260
<i>You've got to try to make yourself explode and do whatever you want.</i>

00:07:54.260 --> 00:07:58.540
<i>Plus, there's not even a one-in-a-million
chance you'll win tomorrow's meet, right?</i>

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:00.270
<i>Make it an adventure!</i>

00:08:01.220 --> 00:08:02.500
Stop exaggerating.

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:04.740
An adventure, huh?

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:10.050
Congratulations on making the finals.

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:15.050
It's okay if you fail in the finals,
but make sure you perform to your heart's content.

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:18.300
<i>Ryou says it, Coach Asaki says it...</i>

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:21.670
<i>But my goal is different from everyone else's.</i>

00:08:21.670 --> 00:08:24.290
<i>Making it through preliminaries was a miracle in itself.</i>

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:26.480
<i>Right, it's because of that jinx.</i>

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:28.690
<i>I had orange juice in the morning,</i>

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:31.690
<i>used an odd-numbered locker,</i>

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:35.210
<i>and entered the meet's venue with my right foot.</i>

00:08:36.340 --> 00:08:40.870
<i>My goal isn't the Olympics or some great prize.</i>

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:42.790
<i>Those things aren't meant for the bottom rungs.</i>

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:44.450
<i>I'm aiming for 11th.</i>

00:08:45.840 --> 00:08:49.210
<i>To do that, I can't let the diver behind me step on my...</i>

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:50.210
<i>shadow!</i>

00:08:50.660 --> 00:08:52.630
<i>Damn it, the jinx is broken.</i>

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:55.720
Not only was it lame, it was a failed dive.

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:57.220
Oh, I'm from Tokushima. My name's—

00:08:57.220 --> 00:08:59.470
Matsuno, let's have an adventure!

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:00.580
Huh?

00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:03.910
Let's blast through with all we've got and break out of our shells!

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:09.730
<i>Start with my right foot...</i>

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:13.530
<i>But who cares about some curse?!</i>

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:18.990
Reiji had an awakening!

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.000
Yamada Atsuhiko

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.000
Ibaraki Spirits

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.000
Back 3.5 Somersault Pike

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:32.170
He's really changed.

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:36.570
I've been watching him since he was smaller than you.

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:40.780
Now that you mention it, he doesn't seem
pointlessly caught up with Youichi this time.

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:43.790
He's probably very committed to this.

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:47.670
With that, perhaps he's overcome his fatal mental weakness.

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:54.780
The finals for the swimming relay have started too.

00:10:29.870 --> 00:10:31.040
Damn it.

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:37.860
For better or for worse, this is the final stretch.

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:38.570
Yeah.

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:40.980
<i>I could turn this around.</i>

00:10:40.980 --> 00:10:43.390
<i>If I can pull off the SS Special...</i>

00:10:44.430 --> 00:10:51.700
<i>Attempting to perfect the technique in two weeks,
training late last night, turning down the representative spot...</i>

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:56.090
<i>Damn it. I've been doing really stupid things.</i>

00:10:58.450 --> 00:11:02.090
<i>If I end up taking diving away from my father...</i>

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:10.260
<i>Please, just let me dive once more.</i>

00:11:10.260 --> 00:11:11.560
<i>I'm begging.</i>

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:13.110
Go, Fujitani.

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:16.110
Hurry and go.

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:18.230
You first.

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:21.860
Believe me, I'd love to.

00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:25.230
Unfortunately, my turn is after yours.

00:11:25.230 --> 00:11:28.100
If you don't jump, neither can I.

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:29.620
Then skip ahead of me.

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:32.180
That I cannot do.

00:11:32.180 --> 00:11:34.480
It's the long awaited Memorial Day, after all.

00:11:34.480 --> 00:11:37.380
I think I'll enjoy it to the very last.

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:38.630
Huh?

00:11:39.150 --> 00:11:43.300
We've faced off countless times up until now.

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:48.140
But today was the first time I beat you in the preliminaries.

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:51.920
I'll be diving after you on the big stage of the finals.

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:55.400
I want to savor this sense of superiority until the very end.

00:11:55.800 --> 00:11:58.250
If you don't go, you'll be disqualified.

00:11:58.250 --> 00:12:00.400
No way. You dive first.

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:02.400
If not, I won't dive.

00:12:02.790 --> 00:12:04.410
I refuse to dive!

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:05.430
Damn it.

00:12:06.050 --> 00:12:07.910
Another idiot, huh?

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:09.990
Look who's talking.

00:12:09.990 --> 00:12:12.050
Now get up there, you fool.

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:20.920
<i>I could still turn this around.</i>

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:25.540
<i>He reminds me of myself.</i>

00:12:27.900 --> 00:12:31.640
Hey, you know <i>Run, Melos</i>? Melos has the best strategy.

00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:32.940
Oh, why is that?

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:41.150
Well, Melos could just save his friends easily with time to spare if he took off right away and ran normally, right?

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:42.120
Yes.

00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:45.610
But in the end, he just barely makes it.

00:12:45.610 --> 00:12:48.200
I think that's definitely a part of his strategy.

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:49.960
What a strategy.

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:52.450
Yeah. Having time to spare isn't allowed.

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:58.910
Melos can't get truly fired up unless it's a last-second struggle and all hope is lost!

00:12:58.910 --> 00:13:03.720
<i>That night, I decided to have him join MDC.</i>

00:13:04.610 --> 00:13:11.030
<i>Now, seven years later,
I've become more of a coach to him than a father.</i>

00:13:12.150 --> 00:13:18.480
If MDC is shut down due to my lack of ability,
there are ways that I'll have to take responsibility for it.

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:20.730
What is that supposed to mean?

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:24.120
Old soldiers never die; they just fade away.

00:13:24.120 --> 00:13:25.740
That's all it is.

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:28.900
You can't mean you're going to
stop being a diving coach, right?

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:33.090
<i>I said something I really shouldn't have...</i>

00:13:53.510 --> 00:13:57.270
Fujitani Youichi, 5255B, 3.6 D.D.

00:13:59.380 --> 00:14:02.420
<i>I can tell you're in bad condition.</i>

00:14:02.420 --> 00:14:04.780
<i>Can you dive in that state?</i>

00:14:05.290 --> 00:14:08.980
Shuurin University has just set a new record for Japan!

00:14:21.240 --> 00:14:23.320
What's Youichi doing?

00:14:23.320 --> 00:14:25.540
That was the warning whistle just now, wasn't it?

00:14:25.540 --> 00:14:28.680
If he doesn't dive within one minute, he'll be disqualified.

00:14:43.640 --> 00:14:45.900
Stop it! Be quiet!

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:49.320
My son... My son is going to dive!

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:04.280
<i>That's right.</i>

00:15:04.280 --> 00:15:07.340
<i>I get fired up when all hope is lost.</i>

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:24.610
Fujitani Youichi

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:24.610
Back 2.5 Somersault 2.5 Twist Pike

00:15:29.090 --> 00:15:32.800
<i>I won't be winning a meet; I'll be winning a battle.</i>

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:39.510
You're okay with this, right?

00:15:39.510 --> 00:15:45.380
I'm sure you know, but since the swan dive is a
low-difficulty dive, you won't earn many points.

00:15:45.680 --> 00:15:47.870
You want to see it, don't you?

00:15:47.870 --> 00:15:53.140
That's why you showed me my gramps' film and had me learn ballet, isn't it?

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:54.350
Yes.

00:15:54.350 --> 00:15:56.430
Then just say that from the start.

00:15:56.430 --> 00:15:58.890
But I don't want you to force yourself.

00:15:59.650 --> 00:16:02.640
You're a huge pain too.

00:16:07.060 --> 00:16:13.140
With my Okitsu blood, I'll put my grandfather's will and my own soul into this dive.

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:18.670
Okitsu Shibuki

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:18.670
Forward Dive Straight

00:16:14.670 --> 00:16:18.670
Okitsu Shibuki, 101A, 1.6 D.D.

00:16:19.860 --> 00:16:22.650
That guy, pulling a trick out of his sleeve at the very end.

00:16:22.650 --> 00:16:24.920
Okitsu is so manly!

00:16:29.440 --> 00:16:30.740
The swan dive...

00:16:31.750 --> 00:16:32.650
<i>Gramps...</i>

00:16:34.020 --> 00:16:35.100
<i>Are you watching?</i>

00:16:36.090 --> 00:16:39.220
<i>Here's my answer!</i>

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:44.730
Okitsu Shibuki

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:44.730
Forward Dive Straight

00:16:51.330 --> 00:16:55.800
<i>It's like Youichi and Okitsu's dives have awakened a dragon.</i>

00:16:56.700 --> 00:17:00.740
<i>That's right. A dragon that I alone have to...</i>

00:17:02.440 --> 00:17:03.250
<i>I can't.</i>

00:17:04.110 --> 00:17:05.940
<i>I can't, I can't, I can't.</i>

00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:08.070
<i>It really is hopeless.</i>

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:11.280
<i>I'm sinking to rock bottom.</i>

00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:13.760
<i>Aim for the top.</i>

00:17:14.580 --> 00:17:17.510
<i>Climb to the highest peak you can.</i>

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:22.150
<i>There's a view only you can see.</i>

00:17:22.150 --> 00:17:24.370
<i>Don't think something's impossible.</i>

00:17:24.370 --> 00:17:26.400
<i>Everyone has the potential.</i>

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:28.460
<i>That's right.</i>

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:30.770
<i>You're exactly right, Youichi.</i>

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:39.120
<i>What I'm aiming for isn't the Olympics or victory.</i>

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:43.690
<i>It's surpassing the limits that I set for myself.</i>

00:17:44.420 --> 00:17:45.540
<i>The four-and-a-half.</i>

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:47.770
<i>That's my limit.</i>

00:17:47.770 --> 00:17:49.180
<i>And I'm gonna surpass that!</i>

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:55.540
<i>Coach Asaki said the four-and-a-half has a success rate of zero percent.</i>

00:17:56.640 --> 00:18:02.220
<i>Keep bringing out the power you have until nothing more will come out,</i>

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:04.560
<i>or you'll never be able to pull off a four-and-a-half.</i>

00:18:04.900 --> 00:18:09.560
<i>If you're exhausted, then bleed, sweat, and throw up stomach acid.</i>

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:11.660
<i>Make that zero into one percent.</i>

00:18:11.660 --> 00:18:13.570
<i>Make that one into two percent.</i>

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:16.380
<i>Don't think something's impossible.</i>

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:18.480
<i>Everyone has the potential.</i>

00:18:18.480 --> 00:18:20.570
<i>That goes for the both of us.</i>

00:18:21.060 --> 00:18:22.990
<i>That's why I'll dive!</i>

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:27.830
<i>This is the new view that no one knows and no one could see</i>

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:29.790
<i>but me!</i>

00:18:43.470 --> 00:18:45.350
A concrete dragon.

00:18:46.840 --> 00:18:48.280
<i>On that one summer day,</i>

00:18:48.280 --> 00:18:55.110
<i>Youichi climbed to the top of the tallest dragon and
was like a hero who vanquished a monster in my eyes.</i>

00:18:56.080 --> 00:18:57.340
<i>Ever since then,</i>

00:18:57.340 --> 00:19:04.120
<i>I was shown this concrete dragon and became addicted to the fear and excitement of this world of wind and water.</i>

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:06.120
<i>Also...</i>

00:19:07.060 --> 00:19:09.760
So tomorrow's finally the day you go to America?

00:19:09.760 --> 00:19:11.630
Wish I could go to America.

00:19:11.630 --> 00:19:14.760
It's not like he's going there to play around.

00:19:14.760 --> 00:19:15.880
I know that.

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:18.130
It'll be lonely without you.

00:19:18.450 --> 00:19:20.040
Knock that crap off.

00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:21.490
It's only half a year.

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:22.710
Only, huh?

00:19:22.710 --> 00:19:25.390
That's right. I guess I should have one last going-away sukiyaki.

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:28.720
Oh, good idea! A final father and son one-on-one.

00:19:28.720 --> 00:19:31.650
Listen, you're not my dad...

00:19:30.610 --> 00:19:31.650
You're late!

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:33.400
Sorry!

00:19:44.130 --> 00:19:45.320
Once more!

00:19:45.320 --> 00:19:47.910
Red, your takeoff was early!

00:19:47.910 --> 00:19:50.660
Green, watch Red's rotation more closely!

00:19:50.970 --> 00:19:55.070
Sheesh. She should've just gone to America with Okitsu.

00:19:55.070 --> 00:19:56.310
I hear you.

00:19:56.980 --> 00:19:59.630
But this really is a bad idea.

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:03.430
What is? Entering the synchronized event at the Olympics with me?

00:20:03.950 --> 00:20:08.300
You better not be thinking of beating me still.

00:20:08.300 --> 00:20:10.930
Is that why you always take off earlier than me?

00:20:10.930 --> 00:20:13.500
No, no. Of course not.

00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:14.690
Then what's the bad idea?

00:20:15.020 --> 00:20:16.520
It's our swimsuits.

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:18.200
Why red and green?

00:20:18.200 --> 00:20:21.190
You picked them out! You said we were going for a Christmas-y look.

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:25.990
But, as Japan's representatives,
I believe some Japanese taste is necessary.

00:20:25.990 --> 00:20:27.740
Might I suggest cheery blossom-colored—

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:30.700
You really do want to change back to Pinky, huh?

00:20:31.440 --> 00:20:32.960
You guys are in perfect sync!

00:20:33.430 --> 00:20:34.710
Stop it! Don't say that!

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:41.210
By the way, they'll be interviewing the representatives today.

00:20:41.560 --> 00:20:42.630
An interview?

00:20:42.630 --> 00:20:45.800
Be sure you can properly introduce yourself.

00:20:45.800 --> 00:20:46.720
Will do!

00:20:47.730 --> 00:20:49.720
A self-introduction, huh?

00:20:50.630 --> 00:20:52.480
I'm Sakai Tomoki.

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:53.660
Um...

00:20:53.660 --> 00:20:55.230
My favorite color is blue.

00:20:56.150 --> 00:20:57.990
My favorite flower is the orchid.

00:20:59.100 --> 00:21:02.740
My favorite animals are dogs, dolphins, and whales.

00:21:04.260 --> 00:21:06.370
What else, what else...

00:21:10.190 --> 00:21:11.240
My passion is...

00:21:13.850 --> 00:21:14.250
diving!
